/* ==========================================================================
   Pixel sky header (px): the shipped header art, the text plates that
   sit on top of it, and the mascot. The static backdrop is
   public/art/background.jpg, drawn once by App as an absolutely
   positioned image that fills the band with object fit cover, so the
   horizon and the house land on the bottom edge and the night sky end
   carries the title plate: image rendering pixelated keeps the art
   crisp and chunky from a phone to a judging table. PixelSky and its
   day and storm scenes are still on disk as an unmounted module, so
   their grid rules and their gated motion stay here for the day the
   header mounts it again. Motion is gated behind prefers-reduced-motion:
   no-preference, matching the rest of the app.
   ========================================================================== */

.px-header {
  position: relative;
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  overflow: hidden;
  min-height: clamp(120px, 12vw, 184px);
  background: #b0d9ff;
  border-bottom: 3px solid var(--rp-paper);
}

/* The shipped header photograph: base path aware, cropped to the band,
   anchored so the horizon and the house read while the darker sky end
   sits under the title plate. */
.px-header__art {
  position: absolute;
  inset: 0;
  display: block;
  width: 100%;
  height: 100%;
  object-fit: cover;
  object-position: center 72%;
  image-rendering: pixelated;
}

