reasoningDetails.text:
Hmm, one problem: `.ax-cell` is `display: grid` with `grid-template-columns: auto minmax(0,1fr)` — the label and glyph in row 1, then count/percent span all columns. With `flex: 1 1 0` and `min-width: 0`, the cell can shrink ✓.

Also `.ax-cell__label` may wrap within its column ✓.

Now the `.ax-detail` styles for the district detail panel. Where to add? Near the cartogram block. I'll add after `.ax-legend__note` (before the mapping rules) or right after the cartogram head/tiles. Let's add a block after `.ax-legend__note` rules (i.e., where the gauge comment used to be).

Design of detail panel:

```html
<div className="ax-detail" role="status" aria-live="polite">
  <p className="ax-detail__name">Hl.m. Praha</p>
  <ul className="ax-detail__bands">
    <li className="ax-detail__band" data-band="critical">
      <span className="ax-detail__label">Critical</span>
      <span className="ax-detail__count">6</span>
    </li>
    ... five  </ul>
  <p className="ax-detail__note">Source data incomplete ...</p>  (no-data case)
</div>
```

Hmm — `role="status"` + aria-live polite announces updates on click ✓. But a role=status region that's hidden until selection... Initially not rendered (null). When it appears, screen readers announce its content ✓.

CSS:
```css
/* District detail: the five band counts for the district the judge
   picked, announced politely when the selection changes. ------------- */

.ax-detail {
  display: grid;
  gap: var(--rp-s2);
  padding: var(--rp-s3);
  background: var(--cp-inset);
  border: 2px solid var(--cp-ink);
  border-left-width: 8px;
  border-left-color: var(--cp-ink);
  box-shadow: 3px 3px 0 0 var(--cp-shadow);
}

.ax-detail__name {
  margin: 0;
  font-family: var(--rp-font-pixel); /* hmm, pixel face is chrome only... it's a district name (chrome-ish) */
  ...
}
```

Wait: index.css says the pixel face is "chrome only: the station title, eyebrows, band names, and button caps. Every number the engine prints stays on the tabular mono stack". The detail panel's counts are numbers → use `--rp-font-display` (tabular mono) ✓. The district name → `--rp-font-utility` uppercase tracked like `.ax-cartogram__title`? Let's check `.ax-cartogram__title` style and mimic.

Let's look at `.ax-cartogram__title` and `.ax-tile__name` for consistency.

Also the five band labels inside detail: uppercase utility font; counts: display font, tabular-nums, colored by band via `--ax-band` mapping (`.ax-shell [data-band=...]` applies if inside .ax-shell ✓ — the detail panel is inside .ax-cartogram which is inside .ax-shell ✓; also `.ax-cartogram [data-band=...]` applies ✓).

Let's write CSS:

```css
/* District detail: name plus the five band counts for the district
   the judge picked, announced politely when the selection changes. -- */

.ax-detail {
  display: grid;
  gap: var(--rp-s2);
  padding: var(--rp-s3);
  background: var(--cp-inset);
  border: 2px solid var(--cp-ink);
  border-radius: var(--cp-radius);
  box-shadow: 3px 3px 0 0 var(--cp-shadow);
}

.ax-detail__name {
  margin: 0;
  font-family: var(--rp-font-display);
  font-weight: 700;
  font-size: 1rem;
  color: var(--cp-ink);
}

.ax-detail__bands {
  display: flex;
  flex-wrap: nowrap;
  gap: var(--rp-s2);
  list-style: none;
  margin: 0;
  padding: 0;
}

.ax-detail__band {
  flex: 1 1 0;
  min-width: 0;
  display: grid;
  gap: 2px;
  padding: var(--rp-s2);
  background: var(--cp-surface);
  border: 2px solid var(--cp-ink);
  border-top: 6px solid var(--ax-band);
}

.ax-detail__label {
  font-family: var(--rp-font-utility);
  font-size: 0.625rem;
  font-weight: 600;
  letter-spacing: 0.1em;
  text-transform: uppercase;
  color: var(--cp-ink-dim);
}

.ax-detail__count {
  font-family: var(--rp-font-display);
  font-weight: 700;
  font-size: 1.125rem;
  font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
  color: var(--ax-band);
}

.ax-detail__note {
  margin: 0;
  font-family: var(--rp-font-body);
  font-size: 0.75rem;
  line-height: 1.5;
  color: var(--cp-ink-faint);
}

@media (max-width: 36rem) {
  .ax-detail__bands {
    flex-wrap: wrap;
  }

  .ax-detail__band {
    flex: 1 1 9rem;
  }
}
```

Note: the detail panel is inside `.ax-cartogram` ✓ so `[data-band]` mapping works.

Careful with dashScan CSS: no ' - ' ✓; check "name plus the five band counts for the district the judge picked" ✓.

Now let's add this CSS right where the gauge comment was (before "/* The five mapping rules again").

